CAR - enter the plugged-in cartridge››Syntax:› CAR [/F|N|I] [/L mode] [d:][path]›     [file] [params]››Starts the cartridge plugged in on top›of the DOS cartridge. With a file name›the file is loaded and run with that›cartridge enabled (e.g. compiled›ACTION! programs).››Options:› /N  return to the cartridge, not to›     DOS, after the program› /I  start cold, skipping the›     memory-save file› /F  run the file even when no ROM is›     seen at $A000› /L  loading mode: S (0, SDX), A (64,›     Atari DOS, the default), N (128,›     no run), I (192, init only) or a›     number››Memory save: when $CAR names a file,›the cartridge's memory is saved there›on leaving with DOS and loaded again›on entry, as BASIC does with $BASIC.››Examples:› SET CAR=D8:CAR.SAV› CAR› CAR /N PROG.COM››See also: BASIC, LOAD, SET›